# Non-English POS priors: resolve on demand with `node scripts/lang-registry.mjs <lang>`.
# Not vendored — nothing reads them yet, and resolved.lock.json (committed) pins
# each source URL + sha256 so a resolve is verifiable and upstream drift is
# reported, never silently absorbed. See POLICIES.md LP10/LP11.
derived-priors/pos-priors/pos-prior-ar.json
derived-priors/pos-priors/pos-prior-es.json
derived-priors/pos-priors/pos-prior-zh.json

# PronunciationPrior@1 WAV bytes: resolve on demand. The MANIFEST
# (derived-priors/pronunciation-priors/pronunciation-<lang>.json) is committed
# — word -> {ipa, sha256, voice, recipe} — and the cache is re-synthesized
# deterministically from it by scripts/build-pronunciation-prior.mjs and the
# lookup API. See the builder header and POLICIES.md LP10/LP11.
derived-priors/pronunciation-priors/cache/
